# Day 37 (Week 6, Day 2): Historical Mix Recommender (from Real Data)

Goal: Given a target compressive strength, search the real UCI dataset 
(1030 lab-tested mixes) for the closest historical matches — a 
practical "reference design" approach used before running new lab 
trials, powered by Day 36's real dataset.
## What I did
- Built a function that filters the real dataset by curing age, then 
  finds the closest matches to a target strength
- Tested with a 40 MPa / 28-day target, returning 5 close historical 
  mixes with actual proportions
- Built a quick-reference table across common strength classes 
  (20-60 MPa)

## Files
- `mix_recommender.py` — main script (reuses Day 36's dataset)

## Result
For a 40 MPa target, the closest real historical mixes achieved 
39.84-40.15 MPa — all within 0.2 MPa of target. Across strength 
classes from 20 to 60 MPa, the closest historical match was always 
within 0.2 MPa of the target, showing the real dataset has good 
coverage across the practical design range.

Status: ✅ Completed
